  {
   "text": "● What happened, from the chat and the card:                                                                                   ",
   "wrapped": false
  },
  {
   "text": "                                                                                                                               ",
   "wrapped": false
  },
  {
   "text": "  - The worker asked one question. You answered \"Stop here\". The worker got it, committed the session log and rewrote its      ",
   "wrapped": true
  },
  {
   "text": "    report, but it kept the state needs-decision with the same question. Dispatch cannot tell a repeated question from a new   ",
   "wrapped": false
  },
  {
   "text": "    one, so the card showed the buttons again.                                                                                 ",
   "wrapped": false
  },
  {
   "text": "  - Your second answer started another run (a reply resumes the session as a copy, so each answer is one more \"Work run\" row on",
   "wrapped": true
  },
  {
   "text": "    the card). That fourth run then ended cleanly with state done.                                                             ",
   "wrapped": true
  },
  {
   "text": "                                                                                                                               ",
   "wrapped": false
  },
  {
   "text": "  So the cause is on both sides: the worker left an answered question in its report, and Dispatch showed it again as new. The  ",
   "wrapped": true
